+/* PSC: the libretro frontend only gets control back on a vertical interrupt (new_vi ->
+ * retro_return), and the VI event is only scheduled once the game has programmed
+ * VI_V_SYNC. A ROM that never gets there (a truncated or corrupt dump that fails IPL3's
+ * checksum and spins) keeps retro_run from ever returning: RetroArch freezes, its menu,
+ * quit and network commands included. So a fallback VI event is queued at power on:
+ * until the game's first VI_V_SYNC write (vi->delay == 0) it only hands control back,
+ * about a frame apart (no screen update, no VI interrupt), and that first write
+ * replaces it with the game's own timing. */
+#define VI_FALLBACK_DELAY 800000
+
